On a terminal the same text is rendered: the heading loses its marker
and the list item trades its dash for a bullet.
<<test functions>>=
def test_print_markdown_renders_on_a_tty(monkeypatch):
  rendered = capture_tty(
    monkeypatch, print_markdown, "# H\n\n- a", indent=2)
  assert "# H" not in rendered
  assert "H" in rendered
  assert "- a" not in rendered
  assert "• a" in rendered
@

Finally the heading substitution: the first line must start with the
heading text itself---no centring spaces, no box drawn with rich's
heavy horizontal rule---and the level-two heading must be left-aligned
too.
<<test functions>>=
def test_notes_markdown_headings_stay_left_and_unboxed():
  console = rich.console.Console(
    file=io.StringIO(), width=40, force_terminal=False)
  console.print(notes_markdown("# Top\n\n## Second\n\ntext"))
  rendered = console.file.getvalue()
  lines = rendered.splitlines()
  assert lines[0].startswith("Top")
  assert "━" not in rendered
  assert any(line.startswith("Second") for line in lines)
